# .beads/issues.jsonl is a FULL-STATE export sorted by id -- NOT append-only.
# Existing lines are modified in place, so this file is NOT safe to merge naively.
#
# union keeps both sides instead of conflicting (the old bd driver silently
# dropped one), but union NEVER CONFLICTS -- it concatenates. When the two sides
# differ on every line (source_repo serialises as null on one machine and "." on
# another) the whole file is one hunk and union DOUBLES IT. edgar-elt went
# 528 -> 1056 rows this way on 2026-08-14.
#
# The doubling is only safe because the post-merge / post-rewrite hooks import
# AND re-export afterwards, and pre-commit hard-fails on duplicate ids:
#     br sync --import-only && br sync --flush-only --force
# Plain --flush-only NO-OPS when no issues are dirty, which is why it must be
# --force there. Install the hooks with cmdrvl-cli/scripts/install-beads-hooks.sh.
# Background and the proper fix: cmdrvl-cli br-1zy4.
.beads/issues.jsonl merge=union
